    {
      "id": "overview",
      "title": "Overview",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "20th century shattered and rebuilt musical language — jazz, serialism, minimalism, recording technology, global fusion."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "movements",
      "title": "Movements",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Impressionism (Debussy, Ravel). Expressionism (Schoenberg, Webern). Neoclassicism (Stravinsky). Minimalism (Reich, Glass)."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "technology",
      "title": "Technology",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Phonograph (1877), radio, LP, cassette, CD, streaming — each transformed how music spreads. Alan Lomax to Spotify."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "trad-revival",
      "title": "Trad revival",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "1960s–70s folk revivals globally. Seán Ó Riada, Bothy Band. Contemporary trad continues evolving with production and fusion."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
